# repro/allocfacts - function facts (G42) read too coarsely for an allocation-free hot path to be pinned while compiling
# (S17a), found pinning ad/graph's Forward and Backward:
# 1. a local fixed array, Array<F32>(8) - laid out in place, which G42's table says does not count - reads Allocates
#    true (lone below; kernels/elem's eight-lane sums are made of these, so every reduction "allocates");
# 2. an error carrying a literal text (an error word of a String payload, as tensor.ShapeError.Mismatch is) reads true,
#    though the text is constant data and the path only ever leaves - so every tensor view taken with `!` "allocates";
# 3. a method of a generic type's instance, `Box<I64>.Fill.Allocates`, is refused by the self-hosted compiler at build
#    ("it does not check a generic name as a value yet"), though G42 names the form - so Graph<F32>.Forward cannot be
#    pinned directly, only through a plain function calling it.
# Expected: the first two asserts hold. Today each is a compile error.
#   olang test repro/allocfacts.olang

fn lone(x Array<F32>&) F32 {
    acc := Array<F32>(8)
    for j in range 8: acc[j] = x[j]
    return acc[3]
}

type Bad error { Mismatch(what String) }

fn checked(x I64) I64 ? Bad {
    if x < 0: error Bad.Mismatch("negative")
    return x
}

assert not lone.Allocates, "a fixed array laid out in place allocates nothing"
assert not checked.Allocates, "an error carrying a literal text allocates nothing"
